      "writtenOn": "2025-10-15T15:43:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I\u0027m not sure why this is here? Seems an adapter like this should go into a `SkXPSPngHelpers.h` something like the existing `SkPDFJpegHelpers.h`.\n\nCan you confirm that you mean having *both* `SkXPSPngRustHelpers.h` and `SkXPSPngLibpngHelpers.h`?  If so, then I can do that.\n\nI guess that those 2 headers could *not* be part of `skia_xps_sources`, because we do *not* want XPS to have a direct dependency on either `libpng` nor Rust PNG.  So those two headers would probably have to belong to `codec.gni`/`skia_codec_rust_png` and `codec.gni/skia_codec_libpng_srcs` (or maybe `skia_codec_rust_png_public` but then `SkPngDecoder.h` is not listed in `codec.gni`...).  Can you please clarify this part as well?\n\n\u003e This would also smooth over some issues later if we needed to actually pass some options along since that implementation could be changed instead of arbitrarily mucking with this one.\n\n\u003e Logically, the issue with that this isn\u0027t really \"default options\" but \"xps options\" which currently happens to be empty (and doesn\u0027t have to be, it should probably be taking a compression level, etc).\n\nMakes sense.",
      "parentUuid": "415b5ec8_944dfc89",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "4f019506b21c36c0cd2344623345530ee659f9c4",
